"epic original" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-original&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-original&gt; element: an item's Original Discussion, its earlier text, folded.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>An item's Original Discussion: the text a rewrite or a second answer replaced, kept so nothing is ever lost. It draws a warm panel headed "Original Discussion", folded, with one <text code>&lt;epic-version&gt;</> inside per earlier version, oldest first.</>

	<!--
		no <ui-list class="spell-meta">:  its <ui-item>s take Spell UI's "item" style sheet name before the
		              epics pack's elements can, and live examples may draw unstyled (issue I9 of epic-components)
	-->
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone reading or writing an epic page's markup, or changing this element.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary (every name it uses): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-original-epicoriginal-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-original/EpicOriginal.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-original/EpicOriginal.en.ts" code>EpicOriginal.en.ts</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-original-epicoriginal-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-original/EpicOriginal.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-original/EpicOriginal.tsx" code>EpicOriginal.tsx</></>, with its style sheet (<text code>.css</>) and tests beside it.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>Two of them; click a heading to unfold it.</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>The first is a real one (from epic <text code>solid-migration</>, T18): one version, dated when it was replaced.</>
			<item>The second holds two versions, so the first is headed "As first written".</>
		</>
		<html>
			<epic-original>
				<epic-version as-of="2026-10-02 23:35">
					<p><b>Title, as first written:</> P11: Solid dev warnings unchanged (seen on HEAD too)</>
					<p>Live, the editor pages log STRICT_READ_UNTRACKED, WIDE_SCOPE_DEPS and HOT_SCOPE_TIME -- before P11 too (checked side by side on the commit before).</>
				</>
			</>
			<epic-original>
				<epic-version>
					<p>Which colours for the review buttons?</>
				</>
				<epic-version as-of="2026-10-04 20:49">
					<p>Which four colours for the review buttons: Fomantic's own?</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>Live: the real element, drawn by the epics pack this page loads.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>Last in its item, before the commits. From <link title="epics/solid-migration/parts/c18.html" target="src-epics-solid-migration-parts-c18-html" link="/epics/solid-migration/parts/c18.html"><text code>c18.html</></>, shortened:</>
		<text paragraph>c18.html · its Original Discussion:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-original
			  ><epic-version as-of="2026-10-02 23:35"
			    ><p><b>Title, as first written:</b> P11: Solid dev warnings unchanged (seen on HEAD too)</p>
			    <p>Live, the editor pages log STRICT_READ_UNTRACKED, ...</p></epic-version
			  ></epic-original
			>
			```
		</>
		<text paragraph>Its place in an item, with the item's other children: <link title="epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md" target="src-spell-epic-src-tool-plan-doc-md" link="/epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md"><text code>PLAN-DOC.md</></>, "Items".</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="map"/>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its parents:</>
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-item-html" link="/epic-item"><text code>&lt;epic-item&gt;</></>: at most one, after the replies and before the commits (an item's children go in a fixed order)</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its children:</>
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-version-html" link="/epic-version"><text code>&lt;epic-version&gt;</></>: one or more, oldest first</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>Everything that reads an item skips it: its option cards are never counted for a pick, and its links are never checked. Ids inside are renamed <text code>data-original-id</>, so no link lands in it.</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<text paragraph>None: its versions carry the dates.</>

		<section label="Slots" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<html>
				<ui-text paragraph>A <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">slot</><ui-popup heading="slot" label="Where the element shows its own children:  the doc's prose, inside its drawing."></> is where the element's own children show.</>
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Slot</>
					<cell>Holds</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>(default)</>
					<cell>The versions.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<html>
				<ui-text paragraph>A <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">part</><ui-popup heading="part" label="A named piece of the element's drawing, which a page's CSS can reach from outside:  epic-note::part(label)."></> is a piece of the drawing a page's CSS can reach.</>
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Part</>
					<cell>Is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>base</>
					</>
					<cell>The panel.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>toggle</>
					</>
					<cell>Its <text code>Original Discussion</> heading, a <text code>&lt;button&gt;</> that folds it.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>body</>
					</>
					<cell>The versions; hidden while folded.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="States" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<html>
				<ui-text paragraph>A <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">state</><ui-popup heading="state" label="A CSS custom state the element sets on itself as it changes:  epic-aside:state(open)."></> is set by the element on itself; none is ever written in the doc.</>
			</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>State</>
					<cell>When</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>open</>
					</>
					<cell>Unfolded. It starts folded.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="5. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>A warm panel, rounded, no border: the brand's ivory (<text code>--epic-aside</> from <text code>&lt;epic-page&gt;</>, with a fallback), as the docs' asides.</>
			<item>No state colour: it's history, nothing to act on.</>
			<item>Its heading is a button: a chevron, then "Original Discussion" in the headings' font. The chevron turns down while it's open.</>
			<item>Folded to start with. Folding is the page's, never written to the doc.</>
			<item>Folded, its body is <text code>hidden="until-found"</>: find-in-page still reaches the text, and unfolds it.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="6. Written by">
		<icon slot="icon" name="terminal"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><text code>epic details &lt;epic&gt;#&lt;id&gt; --file &lt;html&gt;</>: a rewrite of the item's text moves the old text here, as a new version.</>
			<item><text code>decide</> again, and <text code>details ... --more</> again: the answer or More Details they replace.</>
			<item><text code>epic restore &lt;epic&gt;#&lt;id&gt; --file &lt;html&gt; \[--as-of "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM"]</>: text recovered from git (old markup welcome).</>
			<item>The tool makes it when the item has none (<text code>PlanDoc.keepOriginal()</>), and skips a version that says the same as one already there.</>
			<item>The converter (<text code>epic convert</>) turned the old markup's Original Discussion into it (<text code>CardConverter</>).</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
			<ui-divider></>
			<ui-text class="meta" paragraph>Last checked 2026-10-09 against branch <ui-text code>epic-components</>.</>
		</>
	</>
